  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nBy mid week the surface high will be centered near the East Coast\nand a deep-layer ridge is forecast to approach the Mississippi\nValley. Middle Tennessee will see be in warming trend as a \nresult, and afternoon temperatures will be quite pleasant for the \nrest of the week despite chilly overnights. Unfortunately the \nsluggish weather pattern appears to keep meaningful moisture \nreturn to our west with the ridge remaining in place across the \nSoutheast. Rain chances are near zero, though there's some hope in\nensembles for a cold front/light soaking rain on Sunday (PoPs are\n~20%).",
